questions.question_text:
The bottom side is the base.
Which labelled segment is its perpendicular height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (5.4,0);\coordinate (C) at (6.8,3);\coordinate (D) at (1.4,3);\coordinate (H) at (1.4,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {base};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$r$};\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,above] {$s$};\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,left] {$t$};\draw[dashed] (D)--(H) node[midway,right] {$u$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(D)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Side $AB$ is the base.
Which segment is the matching height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (5,0);\coordinate (C) at (3.4,3.2);\coordinate (H) at (3.4,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$AB$};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$j$};\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above left] {$k$};\draw[dashed] (C)--(H) node[midway,right] {$m$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(C)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In this right-angled triangle, $x$ is the chosen base.
Which segment is its height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (R) at (0,0);\coordinate (A) at (4.5,0);\coordinate (B) at (0,3);
\draw (R)--(A) node[midway,below] {$x$};\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above right] {$z$};\draw (B)--(R) node[midway,left] {$y$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(R)!0.3cm!(A)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(R)!0.3cm!(B)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(R)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The base is vertical.
Which labelled segment is its matching height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (0,3.2);\coordinate (C) at (4.5,4.2);\coordinate (D) at (4.5,1);\coordinate (H) at (0,1);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {base};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$a$};\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,right] {$b$};\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,below right] {$c$};\draw[dashed] (H)--(D) node[midway,above] {$d$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(D)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The base $PQ$ is extended.
Which segment is the perpendicular height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);\coordinate (Q) at (3.8,0);\coordinate (R) at (5.2,2.8);\coordinate (H) at (5.2,0);
\draw (P)--(Q) node[midway,below] {$PQ$};\draw (Q)--(R) node[midway,right] {$f$};\draw (R)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$g$};\draw[dashed] (Q)--(H);\draw[dashed] (R)--(H) node[midway,right] {$h$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(R)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(Q)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For the parallelogram shown, which listed pair is a valid base and matching height?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (5,0);\coordinate (C) at (6.3,2.9);\coordinate (D) at (1.3,2.9);\coordinate (H) at (1.3,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below] {$w$};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$x$};\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,above] {$y$};\draw (D)--(A) node[midway,left] {$z$};\draw[dashed] (D)--(H) node[midway,right] {$v$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(D)$);\coordinate (rb) at ($(H)!0.3cm!(B)$);\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(H)$)--(rb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
